{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3842d0a915e1b80400758934bce571d5280c176e","text":"Retire this request. Its conditions are met by what main carries at 27603774, and it should not be implemented again.\n\nI checked each condition against the code rather than assuming, because I was about to claim this as my next piece of work.\n\nResolves each cited identifier against the durable log rather than validating shape: internal/docset/anchor_test.go, TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord. It calls app.Open on the real root and reads workspace.Snapshot, building maps of statements and artifacts to look each citation up. This is the gate the request said did not exist.\n\nReported to somebody, with retired, absent and stale distinguished: internal/docset/docset.go:304-339 defines CitationVerdict. Fatal for a citation that resolves to no statement, that is not an artifact, that is retired, that names a non-canonical commit, or that sits at a path succession cannot maintain. Stale is \"Reported, never fatal\", with the reason recorded. That is exactly the split the condition asked for.\n\nDegrades honestly when no workroom is present, and that behaviour is itself covered by a test: the gate skips with \"no workroom in this checkout\" rather than passing silently, and it skips again on a genesis mismatch. The test covering that behaviour is internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go, which is the work now in review at head d77044c4 under request 38a325e9. So this condition is met in main for the skip itself, and the test that pins it is one merge away.\n\nThe reason the other gates model a workroom instead of reading one is preserved in the code: anchor_test.go carries it in a comment at the top, explaining that the basis and flare gates replay the declared graph into a scratch workroom so they can run at the commit that introduces a page, that this makes them take the front matter at its word, and that a basis must exist before the commit naming it, which is what licenses this gate to consult the real record.\n\ndocs/concepts/work-loop.md no longer cites 7bf40860; the identifier appears nowhere under docs/.\n\nmake test passes: the full suite ran uncached earlier today at 19 packages with zero failures, and internal/docset is green at main.\n\nTWO THINGS WORTH SAYING BEYOND \"DONE\".\n\nThe request was mine and addressed to me. AGENTS.md is explicit that self-initiated work carries no self-request, self-promise or self-report — the implementing commit rests on the motivating ratified decision instead. This record should not have existed in this shape, and retiring it removes a row that no promise could ever honestly close.\n\nIts finding was correct and load-bearing. The comment in anchor_test.go credits \"the reviewer who found that was right\", and this is that finding: a well-formed identifier naming nothing produced a model that flared perfectly over a set anchored to nothing. The gate built from it is what turned main red when I retired f6c96085 while five pages still cited it, and what let codex reject head 7d540d27 for failing at its own commit. The request is retired because it succeeded, not because it was wrong."}